ions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2245976836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2274968194","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518#issuecomment-2274968194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518","id":2274968194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86HmUKC","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-08-08T05:14:53Z","updated_at":"2024-08-08T05:14:53Z","body":"This has some BSD-like text, but definitely it's own variant (and looks to be quite old)\r\n\r\n+1 to add\r\n\r\nGiven that the American Radio Relay League copyright is older and \"ARRL\" is used in various places in the license, I'm wondering if `ARRL' would be a better id?\r\nand maybe American Radio Relay League License for the full name?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2274968194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2275851414","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518#issuecomment-2275851414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518","id":2275851414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86HpryW","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-08-08T13:35:25Z","updated_at":"2024-08-08T13:35:25Z","body":"+1 to add\r\n\r\nLooks like there have been several variations over time for this one. A bit of history from some digging:\r\n\r\n* The [SourceForge history](https://sourceforge.net/p/trustedqsl/tqsl/ci/9efc28c7c6bac0f67ff6c8c3409270415e1f96ad/log/?path=/LICENSE.txt) shows changes over time. For example, [this commit](https://sourceforge.net/p/trustedqsl/tqsl/ci/afe0464c7d0cbce7bdbd8223ec0716f66681795d/) in 2003 removed an advertising clause that was previously present.\r\n* Debian mailing lists in 2003 [discussed one of these earlier versions](https://lists.debian.org/debian-legal/2003/10/msg00329.html) that had 8 clauses, including the advertising clause.\r\n* Fedora mailing lists in 2008 [discussed the same version](https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/legal@lists.fedoraproject.org/thread/QAB6ZMJGZ4HMDZ3CVPF54ZAC2X5L76HA/) that was submitted in this issue. (And I see also now that @richardfontana already noted this in the current Fedora review discussion.)\r\n* Gentoo [also has the same version](https://gitweb.gentoo.org/repo/gentoo.git/tree/licenses/LOTW) that was submitted in this issue, and calls the license \"LOTW\" (presumably for the project \"Logbook of the World\").\r\n\r\nSo, regarding the name:\r\n\r\nGiven the above, I'm sort of inclined to go with `LOTW` for the identifier and \"LOTW License\" as the longer name, mostly to crib from the decision that Gentoo already made?\r\n\r\nBut if folks feel more strongly about using `TrustedQSL`, I'm fine with that, as these all appear to be related.\r\n\r\nI might not go with `ARRL`, mostly out of not knowing whether ARRL as an organization may have released other software under different licenses.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2275851414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2275984217","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518#issuecomment-2275984217","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518","id":2275984217,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86HqMNZ","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-08-08T14:32:43Z","updated_at":"2024-08-08T14:32:43Z","body":"Apparently Logbook of the World refers to an associated dataset of some sort maintained by ARRL, so for that reason I'd be inclined to go with TrustedSQL.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2275984217/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2301589156","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518#issuecomment-2301589156","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2518","id":2301589156,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86JL3ak","user":{"login":"karsten-klein","id":20038021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDM4MDIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20038021?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein","html_url":"https://github.com/karsten-klein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/followers","